  "history": null,
  "answer": "The **ESG section (Section 19)** of ILPA’s DDQ 2.0 covers seven areas:\n\n- **Policy and governance:** responsible-investment policies, standards and commitments, ESG oversight, staff training, and links to performance reviews or compensation.\n- **Fundraising:** formal ESG commitments in fund documents and marketing materials.\n- **Pre-investment:** identifying material ESG risks and opportunities, conducting due diligence, and incorporating findings into investment decisions and deal terms.\n- **Post-investment:** ESG value-creation plans, portfolio-company resources and board oversight, KPIs and targets, exit preparation, and financial and sustainability outcomes.\n- **Reporting and disclosure:** ESG reporting to limited partners, discussion at investor meetings, and management and disclosure of material ESG incidents.\n- **Climate change:** investment-related greenhouse-gas emissions, climate risks, commitments and targets, and TCFD reporting.\n- **Additional information:** topics not otherwise covered—such as human rights, biodiversity and DEI—and the management company’s own ESG practices.\n\nILPA places the more detailed **diversity, equity and inclusion questionnaire in a separate Section 20**. Source: *ILPA DDQ 2.0*, pp. 38–42.",
